Copies read by tests/compat/tp_1.rs (TP.1). Refreshed, and checked against
their sources, by:

  scripts/check-canopy-port.sh [--update] <canopy-checkout> <athome-checkout>

  conf.d/*.toml     canopy grofe/conf.d/ (generated by `canopy grofe generate`)
  keys.tsv          canopy tmux/keys.tsv
  keys-grofe.tsv    canopy grofe/keys.tsv
  config.toml       athome home/dot_config/grofe/config.toml
  user.toml         athome home/dot_config/grofe/user.toml.tmpl, rendered
  user.conf         athome home/dot_config/canopy/user.conf.tmpl, rendered

The two templates are rendered without chezmoi: the lookPath block becomes
/bin/zsh and {{ .chezmoi.homeDir }} becomes ~. user.conf is athome's text as
written, quoted source material. On a machine with no /bin/zsh (a Linux CI
container) the script's load check and tp_1.rs swap that /bin/zsh for the
first of zsh and sh that resolves there, since grofe refuses a default-shell
it cannot run; the copy itself keeps /bin/zsh.

